---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Garage Floor & Driveway Power Washing in Kissimmee | Go Pro"
  description="Remove oil stains, tire marks, mold & algae from garage floors and driveways in Kissimmee & Central Florida. Power washing cost and process."
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "Article",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/garage-driveway-power-washing-kissimmee/#article",
        "headline": "Garage Floor & Driveway Power Washing in Kissimmee",
        "description": "How to clean oil stains, tire marks, mold, and algae from garage floors and driveways in Kissimmee using power washing.",
        "author": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC."
        },
        "publisher": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC.",
          "logo": {
            "@type": "ImageObject",
            "url": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/images/logo.png"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/garage-driveway-power-washing-kissimmee/#breadcrumbs",
        "itemListElement": [
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 1,
            "name": "Home",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 2,
            "name": "Guides",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 3,
            "name": "Garage & Driveway Power Washing",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/garage-driveway-power-washing-kissimmee"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }}
>
  <Header />

  <section class="bg-gopro-charcoal text-white py-16 border-b-4 border-gopro-orange">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <nav class="text-sm mb-6 font-sans">
        <a href="/" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <a href="/guides" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Guides</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <span class="text-white">Garage & Driveway Power Washing</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-4 tracking-tight">Garage & Driveway Power Washing in Kissimmee</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-3xl font-sans">
        Remove oil stains, tire marks, mold & algae from concrete. Power washing cost, process & maintenance for Central Florida driveways and garage floors.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-padding">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6 font-sans">
            Garage floors and driveways in <a href="/areas/kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kissimmee</a> accumulate oil stains, tire marks, mold, algae, and dirt over time. <a href="/services/power-washing" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Power washing</a> removes these stains and restores the concrete's appearance. Here's what works based on 15+ years of cleaning driveways and garage floors in <a href="/areas/central-florida" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Central Florida</a>.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">What Power Washing Removes from Concrete</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Oil and grease stains:</strong> Common in garage floors from cars, lawnmowers, and leaked fluids</li>
            <li><strong>Tire marks:</strong> Rubber residue from tires (especially hot tires on garage floors)</li>
            <li><strong>Mold and algae:</strong> Green or black growth in shaded or damp areas (common in humid Florida)</li>
            <li><strong>Dirt and grime:</strong> General buildup from outdoor elements</li>
            <li><strong>Rust stains:</strong> From metal furniture, tools, or fertilizer runoff</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Power Washing Process for Driveways & Garage Floors</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Step 1: Pre-Treat Oil Stains</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Oil stains don't come out with water pressure alone. We apply a degreaser (biodegradable cleaner) to oil spots, let it sit for 10-15 minutes to break down the oil, then agitate with a stiff brush. Fresh oil stains lift easily; old stains may lighten but not disappear completely.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Step 2: Apply Cleaning Solution</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            For general dirt, mold, and algae, we apply a cleaning solution (sodium hypochlorite or concrete cleaner) across the entire surface. This kills mold and loosens grime. Solution sits for 5-10 minutes.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Step 3: Pressure Wash</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            We use a surface cleaner attachment (rotating bar with dual nozzles) for even cleaning without streaks. Pressure: 3,000-4,000 PSI for concrete driveways and garage floors. The surface cleaner prevents "tiger striping" (uneven lines from a wand). Edges and corners are cleaned with a wand.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Step 4: Rinse & Inspect</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Final rinse removes all cleaner residue. We inspect for stubborn stains and re-treat if needed. Most driveways look 80-90% restored after one wash; deep stains may need a second treatment or sealing.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">What About Deep Oil Stains?</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4 font-sans">
            Deep oil stains that have soaked into porous concrete for years may not fully lift with power washing alone. Options:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Multiple treatments:</strong> Pre-treat, wash, let dry, repeat. Can lighten stains significantly.</li>
            <li><strong>Concrete sealer:</strong> After cleaning, apply a stain-blocking sealer. It won't remove the stain but prevents new stains and makes future cleaning easier.</li>
            <li><strong>Concrete paint or epoxy coating:</strong> Covers stains completely. Popular in garages.</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="bg-gopro-orange/10 border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6 my-8">
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
              <strong>Our take:</strong> Most Kissimmee driveways and garage floors look dramatically better after power washing—mold and algae come off completely, oil stains lighten 50-80%. If you have deep oil stains from years of parking, set realistic expectations. Power washing improves appearance; it won't make old stained concrete look brand new.
            </p>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Cost to Power Wash a Driveway or Garage Floor in Kissimmee</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4 font-sans">
            <strong>Driveway (2-car, ~400-600 sq ft):</strong> $100-$200<br />
            <strong>Large driveway (3-car or long, 800-1,000 sq ft):</strong> $200-$350<br />
            <strong>Garage floor (2-car, ~400-500 sq ft):</strong> $100-$200<br />
            <strong>Both driveway + garage floor:</strong> $200-$400
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Pricing depends on size, stain severity, and whether degreasing or multiple treatments are needed. Heavy oil stains add $50-$100 for extra cleaning. See our <a href="/guides/pressure-washing-cost-kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">power washing cost guide</a> for more pricing.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Mold & Algae on Florida Driveways</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Central Florida humidity encourages mold and algae growth on shaded driveways and garage aprons. Green or black patches appear in damp, shady spots (under trees, along north-facing sides). Power washing with mold-killing cleaner removes it completely. Mold will return over time if the area stays shaded and damp—annual or bi-annual power washing keeps it under control.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Should I Seal My Driveway After Power Washing?</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4 font-sans">
            Sealing concrete driveways and garage floors after power washing provides several benefits:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Prevents oil stains:</strong> Sealer fills pores, so oil sits on the surface instead of soaking in.</li>
            <li><strong>Easier cleaning:</strong> Dirt and grime wash off more easily on sealed concrete.</li>
            <li><strong>Slows mold growth:</strong> Sealed concrete stays cleaner longer.</li>
            <li><strong>Enhances appearance:</strong> Sealer can add a slight sheen or wet look.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            <strong>Cost to seal:</strong> $0.50-$1.50 per sq ft. A 2-car driveway (500 sq ft) costs $250-$750 to seal. Sealer lasts 2-5 years depending on traffic and sun exposure. Not required, but recommended if you want long-term stain protection.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">How Often Should I Power Wash My Driveway?</h2>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>High mold/algae areas (shaded, humid):</strong> Once or twice a year</li>
            <li><strong>Normal driveways (sunny, low growth):</strong> Every 1-2 years</li>
            <li><strong>Garage floors:</strong> Every 1-2 years, or when oil stains accumulate</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Common Questions</h2>
          
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-2 tracking-wide">Will power washing remove all oil stains?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
                Fresh oil stains lift easily. Old, deep stains lighten 50-80% but may not disappear completely. Multiple treatments or sealing after cleaning helps.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-2 tracking-wide">Can power washing damage concrete?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
                No, if done correctly. We use appropriate pressure (3,000-4,000 PSI) and a surface cleaner to avoid etching. Old, crumbling concrete can be damaged by high pressure—we adjust technique for delicate surfaces.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-2 tracking-wide">How long does it take to dry?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
                Concrete driveways and garage floors dry in 2-4 hours in sunny Florida weather, longer in shade or high humidity. You can drive on it as soon as it's dry.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-2 tracking-wide">Do you clean the garage too?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
                Yes. We power wash garage floors, but we don't clean walls or organize items. Move cars, motorcycles, and items off the floor before we arrive.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Power washing driveways and garage floors in Kissimmee removes mold, algae, tire marks, and most oil stains. Cost: $100-$400 depending on size and stain severity. Fresh stains lift easily; old stains lighten but may not disappear. Sealing after washing prevents future stains. Annual or bi-annual cleaning keeps concrete looking good in humid Central Florida.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-8 my-8">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide">Need Your Driveway or Garage Power Washed?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-6">
              We power wash driveways, garage floors, and concrete in Kissimmee, Orlando, and Central Florida. Free estimates.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
              <a href="/estimate" class="btn-primary">
                Get Free Estimate
              </a>
              <a href="tel:4072446873" class="btn-secondary">
                Call (407) 244-6873
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 font-sans">
              <a href="/guides" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">← Back to All Guides</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    title="Driveway & Garage Floor Power Washing"
    description="Remove oil stains, mold, algae. Professional cleaning. Serving Kissimmee, Orlando & Central Florida."
  />

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
